(6140451, 904156, 33736, '<td valign="top">Hluboka is a monumental Romantic chateau - originally a Gothic castle - remoted in the Baroque style in 18th century. Later it underwent a significant transformation in the 19th century when it was remodeled in the English Windsor-style Gothic into the official seat of the Schwarzenberg dynasty.  Czech.<br/> <br/>Discovered info online because the hidden info in the image ID at least mentioned the name of the place.</td>', 'Hluboka is a monumental Romantic chateau - originally a Gothic castle - remoted in the Baroque style in 18th century. Later it underwent a significant transformation in the 19th century when it was remodeled in the English Windsor-style Gothic into the official seat of the Schwarzenberg dynasty.  Czech. Discovered info online because the hidden info in the image ID at least mentioned the name of the place.', '2010-08-25 09:00:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(6140454, 904007, 73250, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your ribbon David!! Beautiful image and well deserved score!!</td>', 'Congrats on your ribbon David!! Beautiful image and well deserved score!!', '2010-08-25 09:01:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(6140455, 904194, 33736, '<td valign="top">Pretty cool building, but what is it, and where is it located?<br/></td>', 'Pretty cool building, but what is it, and where is it located?', '2010-08-25 09:04:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(6140457, 904117, 33736, '<td valign="top">What building is this, and where is it located?</td>', 'What building is this, and where is it located?', '2010-08-25 09:09:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(6140460, 904194, 58785, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Kathy:</b></div><hr/><i> Pretty cool building, but what is it, and where is it located? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>This is the Rio Vista Activity Center in Peoria. I didn''t take the whole thing because it doesn''t look as interesting as this angle. My goal was to show only the structure,and that''s about it. Kids called that "Toothpicks", pretty interesting architectural "thing" holds the roof.<br/> <br/><img alt="'' . substr(''//www.peoriaaz.gov/uploadedImages/rio1.jpg'', strrpos(''//www.peoriaaz.gov/uploadedImages/rio1.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.peoriaaz.gov/uploadedImages/rio1.jpg"/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-08-25 08:15:49.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Kathy: Pretty cool building, but what is it, and where is it located?   This is the Rio Vista Activity Center in Peoria. I didn''t take the whole thing because it doesn''t look as interesting as this angle. My goal was to show only the structure,and that''s about it. Kids called that "Toothpicks", pretty interesting architectural "thing" holds the roof. ', '2010-08-25 09:14:08.000000', '2010-08-25 09:15:49.000000', 0),
